:null,"evidence":["ticket_planner._existing_identities returns `set(binding_view) | set(local_snapshot) | set(remote_snapshot)` — the identity namespace a dependency must match to be considered available.","_effective_create_providers keys create targets by identity; a requires_parent value in the wrong namespace (e.g. local_id vs jira_key) is never in `available`, so _dependency_blocked either always fires or never fires.","The inbound conversion at run_differs.py:509-540 keys target=im.jira_key while carrying local_id in payload — two candidate namespaces for the same entity, so which one requires_parent must reference is load-bearing and unstated."],"finding":"The plan does not specify how an emitted requires_parent/requires_create identity is namespaced so it matches what the planner treats as a satisfiable prerequisite, risking an edge that silently no-ops (never orders) or permanently blocks.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f052423f0e7279ed5","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Acceptance Criteria line 1","norm_id":"n3b2ebdb93a82ad2b","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A parent create emits its identity in one namespace while the child's requires_parent references the other — the planner cannot match them and the child is either never held or never released."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive the builder inventory via find_referencing_symbols on the Mutation/create constructor plus a name grep, and add the omitted create-Mutation construction sites (outbound_pass.py:257-270 and binding_walk.py:305-317) to Scope, replacing the mis-cited run_differs.py:568 config-block line.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'production builders at run_differs.py:568 and create_route.py:210-216 do not emit them'","run_differs.py:66-74: 'the self-contained outbound sub-pass driver (_run_differs_outbound) was extracted to the sibling outbound_pass module ... from rebar_reconciler.outbound_pass import _run_differs_outbound'","outbound_pass.py:258-270 constructs the outbound create Mutation (`action=mut_mod.MutationAction.create`, `payload=OutboundCreatePayload(...)`)","binding_walk.py:306-317 constructs a create Mutation on the ADOPT branch","run_differs.py:568-571 is `_max_acting_fraction = compose_config().reconciler.max_acting_fraction` inside try/except — not a Mutation constructor"],"finding":"The plan's affected-file/patch-site inventory for the production mutation builders is incomplete. It names `run_differs.py:568` and `create_route.py:210-216` as the builders that fail to emit `requires_create`/`requires_parent`, but the actual outbound create-Mutation constructor was extracted OUT of run_differs into `outbound_pass._run_differs_outbound` (outbound_pass.py:257-270; run_differs.py:66-74 merely re-exports it). run_differs.py:568 is the binding-walk `max_acting_fraction` config block, not a mutation builder. Two constructing sites are omitted from Scope entirely: outbound_pass.py:257-270 and binding_walk.py:305-317.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe8c05951167c2fbf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem ('production builders at run_differs.py:568 and create_route.py:210-216') and Scope ('run_differs.py, create_route.py, planner, and batch dispatch')","norm_id":"n30769fe1bb9a449c","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["outbound_pass.py:257-270 — the real outbound create-Mutation builder (`Mutation(action=MutationAction.create, payload=OutboundCreatePayload(...))`); not in Scope, so the create/parent edge is never attached to the operation that actually reaches dispatch, and a parent+child created in one outbound pass still reaches Jira unordered.","binding_walk.py:305-317 — the ADOPT-path create Mutation (invoked by run_differs.py:583 via compute_binding_walk_mutations); not in Scope, so any create it emits carries no requires_create/requires_parent.","run_differs.py:568 (the cited 'builder' line) is a try/except around compose_config().reconciler.max_acting_fraction — patching it emits no metadata onto any Mutation, so following the cited location literally under-delivers the change."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Update Context and Scope to name the real create builders: outbound_pass._run_differs_outbound (outbound_pass.py:257-270), binding_walk.py ADOPT branch (305-317), and the create_route coordinated-create path; drop or correct the run_differs.py:568 citation, which is the max_acting_fraction config block rather than a mutation constructor.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_cla