hen the dependent op is reached"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add to Approach/Testing: 'When a dependent op's requires_parent mapping is absent at dispatch time, the dispatcher raises/records an explicit error rather than applying the child; the missing-parent-mapping test asserts this failure surface.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"State the failure-disposition contract for the 'missing parent mapping' arm: does the blocked child surface as retryable/transient (held for a later pass) or fatal/permanent (skipped), and assert that disposition in the dispatcher test.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Testing: 'missing parent mapping' is listed as a scenario","AC3: 'Dispatcher coverage proves the child does not apply before its parent mapping exists' — states the negative (does not apply) but not what disposition surfaces when the parent mapping is permanently absent (e.g. parent create failed upstream)","ABSENCE: no explicit disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) attached to the child-blocked-by-missing-parent arm"],"finding":"The plan exercises the 'missing parent mapping' case (a child operation whose parent create edge cannot be satisfied at dispatch time) but never states the disposition the caller surfaces on that arm — whether the dependent child is deferred/held-back as retryable/transient, or skipped/failed as fatal/permanent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc556d1c322a38d03","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section ('missing parent mapping') and Acceptance Criteria line 3","norm_id":"nf9d389a8fbc36fbc","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A parent create fails or is dropped, so its mapping never materializes; the dependent child reaches dispatch with an unsatisfiable requires_parent edge and the caller cannot tell whether to retry the batch or treat the child as permanently unappliable"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to Testing/Acceptance: 'When a child's required parent mapping is absent at dispatch, the child operation is held as retryable (transient) rather than applied or silently dropped; dispatcher coverage asserts this disposition.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severit